// MASTER COPY - this is the tracked one.  The build copies it to
// Run/Data/Patch.str, which is where the game reads it from and which is
// gitignored, so edit THIS file and rebuild (or copy it across by hand).
//
// Patch.str is the 1.04 string overlay from PatchData.big.  The two original
// strings are kept; everything after them is this fork's.
//
// Comments are '//' - GameText.cpp parseStringFile skips exactly that.

GUI:CustomMission
"CUSTOM MISSION"
END

GUI:StartCustomMission
"START GAME"
END

GUI:Stop
"Stop"
END

GUI:StopDescription
"Stops what the selected units are doing."
END

// The command grid's own attack, hold position and move keys, which stand in no command set:
// the cards they show under the pointer.

GUI:OrderForceAttackDescription
"The next click attacks whatever is under the pointer, the ground and your own side included. Click the key again to call it off."
END

CONTROLBAR:ForceAttack
"&Force Attack"
END

CONTROLBAR:ToolTipForceAttack
"The next click attacks whatever is under the pointer, the ground and your own side included. Click the button again to call it off."
END

// the idle buttons at the right end of the command grid, under EA's idle worker

CONTROLBAR:IdleInfantry
"Idle Infantry"
END

CONTROLBAR:IdleInfantryDescription
"Click to select the next idle infantry. Shift-click selects all of them. Right-click selects all your infantry, idle or not: those on screen first, the whole map on a second right-click."
END

CONTROLBAR:IdleVehicle
"Idle Vehicle"
END

CONTROLBAR:IdleVehicleDescription
"Click to select the next idle ground vehicle. Shift-click selects all of them. Right-click selects all your ground vehicles, idle or not: those on screen first, the whole map on a second right-click."
END

CONTROLBAR:IdleAircraft
"Idle Aircraft"
END

CONTROLBAR:IdleAircraftDescription
"Click to select the next idle aircraft. Shift-click selects all of them. Right-click selects all your aircraft, idle or not: those on screen first, the whole map on a second right-click."
END

CONTROLBAR:SelectArmy
"Select Army"
END

CONTROLBAR:SelectArmyDescription
"Click to select every fighting unit on screen; click again for your whole army across the map. Workers, supply trucks and buildings are left out."
END

CONTROLBAR:LastAlert
"Last Alert"
END

CONTROLBAR:LastAlertDescription
"Click to move the camera to the last radar alert, such as your base under attack. Click again soon after to go one alert further back."
END

CONTROLBAR:IdleWorkerDescription
"Click to select the next idle worker. Shift-click selects all of them."
END

GUI:OrderHoldPositionDescription
"The selected units guard the spot they stand on and fight whatever comes near, without chasing it out of the area."
END

GUI:OrderMoveDescription
"The next click on the ground sends the selected units there. Drag instead and they spread out along the line you draw."
END

GUI:SelectionTypeDescription
"Click to keep only these selected. Shift-click to take them out of the selection."
END

GUI:OrderStanceDefensiveDescription
"The selected units shoot what comes into range and hold the ground you put them on. Click to make them aggressive: they go after any enemy they see."
END

GUI:OrderStanceAggressiveDescription
"The selected units go after any enemy they see and chase it. Click to make them defensive again: they only shoot what comes into range and stay where they are."
END

// Smoke signals.  The three ...Placed lines are what an ally reads; %s is the sender's name.  The
// ...Label words are written over the smoke, which is in the sender's colour.
GUI:SignalAttack
"Signal: Attack"
END

GUI:SignalDefend
"Signal: Defend"
END

GUI:SignalAttention
"Signal: Look Here"
END

GUI:SignalAttackPlaced
"%s: attack here!"
END

GUI:SignalDefendPlaced
"%s: defend here!"
END

GUI:SignalAttentionPlaced
"%s: look here!"
END

// The money request's line in the allies' chat, in the asker's own language.
GUI:RequestMoneyChat
"I need money!"
END

GUI:GamePaused
"Game paused."
END

GUI:GameResumed
"Game resumed."
END

// The replay strip's pause button while the replay is paused.
GUI:ReplayResume
"Resume"
END

// Skirmish lobby: an opponent seat with no AI behind it (Shift-Ctrl-T takes it over).
GUI:HumanSlot
"Human"
END

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Options screen.  The five page buttons across the top.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GUI:OptionsTabDisplay
"Display"
END

GUI:OptionsTabAudio
"Audio"
END

GUI:OptionsTabControls
"Controls"
END

GUI:OptionsTabInterface
"Interface"
END

GUI:OptionsTabNetwork
"Network"
END

GUI:OptionsTabGraphics
"Graphics"
END

GUI:OptionsTabEffects
"Effects"
END

GUI:Ultra
"Ultra"
END

GUI:TreeSway
"Swaying Trees"
END

TOOLTIP:TreeSway
"Trees and shrubs lean in the wind. Applies from the next map."
END

TOOLTIP:ExtraAnimations
"Buildings rise inside scaffolding while they are built. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:ExtraAnimations
"Building Scaffolding"
END

GUI:Detail
"Detail Preset"
END

GUI:GraphicsQuality
"Performance / Quality"
END

TOOLTIP:GraphicsQuality
"Left is the fastest picture, right the best looking. Dragging it sets the boxes on this page and on Effects, the cheap ones first, and the four presets are points along it. Change a box afterwards and the preset reads Custom. Applies when you press Accept; some settings wait for the next map or the next launch."
END

GUI:DetailNote0
"Every box on, the most particles and thick smoke, and detail never drops in a big fight. Picking it only fills in the boxes; Accept applies it."
END

GUI:DetailNote1
"All the shadows and full-size textures, with the original smoke. Picking it only fills in the boxes; Accept applies it."
END

GUI:DetailNote2
"Flat shadows in place of cast ones and fewer particles, for a modest graphics card. Picking it only fills in the boxes; Accept applies it."
END

GUI:DetailNote3
"No shadows, half-size textures and the fewest particles, for an old machine. Picking it only fills in the boxes; Accept applies it."
END

GUI:DetailNote4
"Your own mix of the boxes on this page and on Effects, or a point on the slider between two presets. Accept keeps it as it is."
END

GUI:Shadows3D
"Cast Shadows"
END

TOOLTIP:Shadows3D
"Shadows that units, buildings and trees throw on the ground and on each other. Off turns all of them off, the sun's shadows included, and Infantry Shadows needs it on. Applies when you press Accept; a few shadows only change on the next map."
END

GUI:Shadows2D
"Flat Shadows"
END

TOOLTIP:Shadows2D
"The flat dark patch drawn under a unit or a missile that has no cast shadow. Costs little. Applies when you press Accept."
END

TOOLTIP:CloudShadows
"Cloud shadows drift across the ground. Costs little. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:GroundLighting
"Ground Pattern"
END

TOOLTIP:GroundLighting
"A faint pattern of light and dark laid over the ground, so its repeating tiles show less. Costs little. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:SmoothWater
"Soft Shorelines"
END

TOOLTIP:SmoothWater
"Water fades out at the shore instead of ending on a hard line. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:ShowProps
"Trees And Bushes"
END

TOOLTIP:ShowProps
"Trees and bushes on the map. Off helps a slow machine. Network games always show them. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:HeatEffects
"Heat Haze"
END

TOOLTIP:HeatEffects
"Hot air shimmers, as it does over the Microwave Tank's beam. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:BehindBuilding
"Units Behind Buildings"
END

TOOLTIP:BehindBuilding
"A unit hidden behind a building shows through it as a silhouette in its player's colour. Applies when you press Accept."
END

TOOLTIP:NoDynamicLOD
"When the frame rate drops in a big fight, the game thins out effects to keep up. On, it never does: the picture stays full and the frame rate takes the hit."
END

TOOLTIP:LowResSlider
"How sharp the textures are. Lower saves graphics memory on an old card. Applies when you press Accept."
END

TOOLTIP:ParticleCapSlider
"How many particles of smoke, fire and sparks can exist at once. Big fights reach the limit first; lower it if explosions slow the game down. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:TextureFilter
"Texture Filtering"
END

GUI:TextureFilter0
"Bilinear"
END

GUI:TextureFilter1
"Trilinear"
END

GUI:TextureFilter2
"Anisotropic"
END

TOOLTIP:TextureFilter
"How textures are sampled as they recede from the camera. Bilinear is what the game shipped with and makes distant ground shimmer; anisotropic keeps it sharp. Applies the next time the game starts."
END

GUI:Anisotropy
"Anisotropic Samples"
END

TOOLTIP:Anisotropy
"How many samples anisotropic filtering may take. Auto lets the graphics card decide, up to 16. Only used when texture filtering is anisotropic. Applies the next time the game starts."
END

GUI:AnisotropyCardMaximum
"Auto"
END

GUI:TextureResolution
"Texture Resolution"
END

GUI:ParticleLimit
"Particle Limit"
END

GUI:NeverLowerDetail
"Never Lower Detail"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupScreen
"Screen"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupPicture
"Picture"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupDetail
"Quality"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupEffects
"Effects"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupImage
"Image"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupVolume
"Volume"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupCamera
"Camera"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupPlacement
"Building Placement"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupLighting
"Light And Glow"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupOrders
"Mouse And Orders"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupBattlefield
"Battlefield"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupAddresses
"Addresses"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupFirewall
"Firewall"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupProxy
"Proxy"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupShadows
"Shadows"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupExtras
"Extras"
END

GUI:OptionsGroupParticles
"Smoke And Particles"
END

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// One GUI: label and one TOOLTIP: line per row of TheOptionCatalog.  A label
// and the combo box under it share the tooltip; an OPTION_ENUM row also needs
// its entries, numbered from zero in the order the enum declares them.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GUI:WindowMode
"Window Mode"
END

GUI:WindowMode0
"Fullscreen"
END

GUI:WindowMode1
"Borderless"
END

GUI:WindowMode2
"Windowed"
END

TOOLTIP:WindowMode
"Fullscreen covers the monitor at the resolution above, scaled up to it when smaller, and steps aside on alt-tab. Borderless always draws at the monitor's own resolution and stays put behind other windows."
END

GUI:ResolutionNote0
"Monitor supports this mode"
END

GUI:FullscreenScaling
"Fullscreen Fit"
END

GUI:FullscreenScaling0
"Stretch to fill"
END

GUI:FullscreenScaling1
"Keep shape, add bars"
END

TOOLTIP:FullscreenScaling
"How fullscreen fills a monitor whose shape your resolution does not have, such as 1920x1080 on a 1920x1200 screen or 1024x768 on a widescreen. Stretch fills every pixel; the other keeps the picture's proportions with black bars."
END

GUI:Monitor
"Monitor"
END

TOOLTIP:Monitor
"The monitor the game plays on. The resolution list below holds the sizes this monitor can show. Applied when you Accept."
END

GUI:MSAA
"Antialiasing"
END

GUI:MSAA0
"Off"
END

GUI:MSAA1
"2x"
END

GUI:MSAA2
"4x"
END

GUI:MSAA3
"8x"
END

GUI:MSAA4
"16x"
END

TOOLTIP:MSAA
"Smooths the stair steps along model edges. Only the Direct3D 9 renderer uses it: the default renderer smooths edges on its own and ignores this setting. A level your card does not offer drops to the highest one it does. Applies the next time the game starts."
END

GUI:Bloom
"Glow"
END

GUI:Bloom0
"Off"
END

GUI:Bloom1
"Low"
END

GUI:Bloom2
"Medium"
END

GUI:Bloom3
"High"
END

GUI:Bloom4
"Ultra"
END

TOOLTIP:Bloom
"How hard fire, explosions, muzzle flashes and lasers burn and how far their light spills over what is around them. Buildings, the sky, snow and sand never glow. Off is the look the artwork was painted for. The Direct3D 9 renderer gets a softer version, and under Classic Graphics only the laser halos follow it."
END

GUI:VSync
"Vertical Sync"
END

TOOLTIP:VSync
"Holds the picture to the monitor so it does not tear. Off, the picture runs as fast as the machine draws. Applied when you Accept."
END

GUI:FrameRateLimit
"Frame Rate Limit"
END

GUI:FrameRateLimit0
"Off"
END

GUI:FrameRateLimit1
"240 FPS"
END

GUI:FrameRateLimit2
"144 FPS"
END

GUI:FrameRateLimit3
"120 FPS"
END

GUI:FrameRateLimit4
"60 FPS"
END

TOOLTIP:FrameRateLimit
"The most pictures a second the game draws, in a match and in the menus. A lower limit keeps the graphics card cooler and quieter and does not slow the game down. Off runs a match as fast as the machine draws and holds the menus at 60."
END

GUI:ClassicGraphics
"Classic Graphics"
END

TOOLTIP:ClassicGraphics
"The game as it looked in 2003: its own textures and ground, the old hard shadows, no bump detail and no glow or sharpening. The game opens this way. Untick it for the Reforged picture: the High preset fills in the boxes, and you can move the slider from there. Takes effect the next time the game starts."
END

GUI:DetailedModels
"Detailed Models"
END

TOOLTIP:DetailedModels
"The rebuilt units and buildings, for the Reforged picture, when you downloaded them. They change only what you see: you play with anyone, whether they have them or not. Untick it for a higher frame rate in big battles. Takes effect the next time the game starts."
END

GUI:FullDetailAtDistance
"Full Detail at Distance"
END

TOOLTIP:FullDetailAtDistance
"The rebuilt units and buildings swap to lighter versions as they get small on the screen. Tick it to draw every one at full detail however far the camera is, at some cost to the frame rate in big battles. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:OptionsGroupModels
"Models"
END

GUI:HDTextures
"HD Textures"
END

TOOLTIP:HDTextures
"Every texture and ground tile at twice the detail, for the Reforged picture, when you downloaded them. They change only what you see: you play with anyone, whether they have them or not. Untick it on a card short of video memory. Takes effect the next time the game starts."
END

GUI:InfantryShadows
"Infantry Shadows"
END

TOOLTIP:InfantryShadows
"Soldiers and the other animated models cast real shadows too. Needs Cast Shadows. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:ProjectileShadows
"Missile Shadows"
END

TOOLTIP:ProjectileShadows
"Missiles and bombs the artists gave no shadow get one on the ground. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:PropShadows
"Scenery Shadows"
END

TOOLTIP:PropShadows
"Fences, rubbish and shrubs, which the original drew with no shadow at all, get one. Applies from the next map."
END

GUI:ParticleShadows
"Smoke Shadows"
END

TOOLTIP:ParticleShadows
"Big clouds of smoke and dust lay a soft shadow on the ground under them. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:Smoke
"Smoke"
END

GUI:Smoke0
"Original"
END

GUI:Smoke1
"Thick"
END

GUI:Smoke2
"Very Thick"
END

TOOLTIP:Smoke
"How long smoke hangs in the air and how dense it looks. 175 of the game's 1088 effects are smoke. Very Thick cost 0.7 ms a frame over a burning column when it was measured. Takes effect the next time the game starts."
END

GUI:ParticleBounce
"Particles Hit The Ground"
END

TOOLTIP:ParticleBounce
"Sparks, debris and the other particles land and bounce on the terrain instead of falling through it. Takes effect the next time the game starts."
END

GUI:MiddleMousePans
"Middle Mouse Pans"
END

TOOLTIP:MiddleMousePans
"Hold the middle button to drag the map under the cursor."
END

GUI:ZoomToCursor
"Zoom To Cursor"
END

TOOLTIP:ZoomToCursor
"The wheel zooms towards whatever the cursor is over instead of the middle of the screen."
END

GUI:StartAtMaxZoom
"Start Zoomed Out"
END

TOOLTIP:StartAtMaxZoom
"A match opens with the camera as far out as the wheel goes. Off, it opens close in, at the height the original game used."
END

GUI:ScrollSpeed
"Camera Scroll Speed"
END

TOOLTIP:ScrollSpeed
"How fast the camera pans: at the screen edge, on the arrow keys and while you drag with the right mouse button. The mouse wheel has its own Zoom Speed. Takes effect on Accept."
END

GUI:ZoomSpeed
"Zoom Speed"
END

TOOLTIP:ZoomSpeed
"How far one turn of the mouse wheel moves the camera in or out. At 100 it moves as far as in the original game. Takes effect on Accept."
END

GUI:DragTolerance
"Drag Threshold"
END

TOOLTIP:DragTolerance
"How many pixels the mouse may move with a button held before a click becomes a drag. Raise it if selection boxes start by accident, lower it if drags read as clicks."
END

GUI:AmbientVolume
"Ambient Volume"
END

TOOLTIP:AmbientVolume
"Birds, wind, water and the hum of a town. Sound FX no longer moves these, so the battle can stay loud while the world around it stays quiet."
END

GUI:MasterVolume
"Master Volume"
END

TOOLTIP:MasterVolume
"Turns the whole game up or down: music, effects, voices, ambience and movies. The other sliders keep the mix, this one sets how loud the mix is."
END

GUI:OptionsGroupMusic
"Music"
END

GUI:DynamicMusic
"Music Follows the Fight"
END

TOOLTIP:DynamicMusic
"In a skirmish or online match the music answers the battle: one of your side's calmer tracks while nothing happens, a harder one once guns fire near the camera or at your forces, and back to calm a few seconds after the fight ends. Off leaves the music as the original game played it."
END

GUI:OptionsGroupOutput
"Output"
END

GUI:AudioDevice
"Output Device"
END

TOOLTIP:AudioDevice
"The speakers or headphones the game plays through. Default follows Windows and moves with it when you plug in a headset. Applied when you Accept."
END

GUI:AudioDeviceDefault
"Default"
END

GUI:SpeakerType
"Speaker Setup"
END

TOOLTIP:SpeakerType
"How the battlefield's sounds are placed around you. Headphones give each ear its own timing and tone, so a sound behind or beside you is heard there. 5.1 and 7.1 spread them over surround speakers; on Linux and macOS they play as stereo. Applied when you Accept."
END

GUI:SpeakerType0
"Stereo Speakers"
END

GUI:SpeakerType1
"Headphones"
END

GUI:SpeakerType2
"5.1 Surround"
END

GUI:SpeakerType3
"7.1 Surround"
END

GUI:MuteInBackground
"Mute in Background"
END

TOOLTIP:MuteInBackground
"Silences the game while another window has the focus. Off keeps it playing behind a browser or on a second monitor."
END

GUI:LegacySound
"Legacy Sound"
END

TOOLTIP:LegacySound
"The original game's sound: no pitch bend on passing sounds, no Aurora sonic boom, no cap on battle sounds or unit replies, no limiter, no map ambience and no music following the fight. Master volume, the device and the speakers still apply. Takes effect at once."
END

GUI:CameraShake
"Camera Shake"
END

TOOLTIP:CameraShake
"Blasts shake the camera. A nuke or a big building coming down nearby kicks it hard for a moment. Untick to keep the view still. Applies when you press Accept."
END

GUI:IsometricCamera
"Isometric Camera"
END

TOOLTIP:IsometricCamera
"The battlefield seen from far off, so a unit is the same size at the top of the screen as at the bottom. You still turn and zoom the camera."
END

GUI:EdgeScrollWindowed
"Edge Scroll In A Window"
END

TOOLTIP:EdgeScrollWindowed
"Retail refuses to scroll from the screen edge in windowed mode. Turn this on to get it back on a second monitor or in borderless."
END

GUI:SnapCamera45
"Snap Camera Rotation"
END

TOOLTIP:SnapCamera45
"Rotating the camera clicks to the eight 45 degree headings instead of stopping anywhere. Hold Shift while turning to get the other behaviour for that turn."
END

GUI:GridBuild
"Grid Building Placement"
END

TOOLTIP:GridBuild
"Structures land on the pathfinder's own 10-unit grid, drawn under the building while you place it, so two buildings put down by eye share an edge instead of leaving a gap too narrow to walk through. Off, only the cells nothing can be built on are marked."
END

GUI:NudgeBuild
"Nudge Blocked Placement"
END

TOOLTIP:NudgeBuild
"A structure whose spot is blocked slides to the nearest one it fits instead of going red under the cursor."
END

GUI:SnapBuild45
"Snap Building Rotation"
END

TOOLTIP:SnapBuild45
"Drag-to-rotate clicks to the eight 45 degree headings, which is what walls and defenses along a base edge want."
END

GUI:SnapBuildNeighbour
"Snap to Nearby Buildings"
END

TOOLTIP:SnapBuildNeighbour
"A structure put down a cell or so short of another one is pulled flush against its edge, so the two leave no gap."
END

GUI:RangeRing
"Placement Range Ring"
END

TOOLTIP:RangeRing
"Draws the weapon range of the structure you are about to place."
END

GUI:WorkersReturn
"Workers Return To Supply"
END

TOOLTIP:WorkersReturn
"A worker that finishes a building goes back to gathering instead of standing where it built."
END

GUI:BuildTooltips
"Detailed Build Tooltips"
END

TOOLTIP:BuildTooltips
"Build buttons list cost, build time and prerequisites."
END

GUI:HudOverlay
"HUD Overlay"
END

TOOLTIP:HudOverlay
"The extra readouts across the top of the screen: power, income and the production strip."
END

GUI:NetBox
"Info Box"
END

TOOLTIP:NetBox
"The box in the top right corner with the match clock, the frame rates and the connection. Off, the superweapon timers move up into the corner."
END

GUI:MinimapSize
"Minimap Size"
END

TOOLTIP:MinimapSize
"How big the minimap is drawn. Above 100 it grows up from the bottom left corner over the battlefield; the rest of the command bar stays as it is."
END

GUI:OptionsGroupHud
"HUD"
END

GUI:EmptyBuildingPips
"Empty Building Slots"
END

TOOLTIP:EmptyBuildingPips
"The row of empty slots over a building with nobody inside, like the ten over a Tunnel Network. Off, a building shows its slots only while someone is in it."
END

GUI:HitFlash
"Hit Flash"
END

TOOLTIP:HitFlash
"A unit or building that takes damage lights up red for a moment, so you see what is being shot at."
END

GUI:DamageNumbers
"Damage Numbers"
END

TOOLTIP:DamageNumbers
"The damage a hit does rises over the unit in red."
END

GUI:IdleWorkerCamera
"Jump to Idle Worker"
END

TOOLTIP:IdleWorkerCamera
"The idle worker button and key move the camera to the worker."
END

GUI:ArchiveReplays
"Archive Replays"
END

TOOLTIP:ArchiveReplays
"Every game is kept under its own name instead of overwriting the last one."
END

GUI:HealthBars
"Health Bars"
END

GUI:HealthBars0
"Always"
END

GUI:HealthBars1
"Smart"
END

GUI:HealthBars2
"Selection Only"
END

GUI:HealthBars3
"Never"
END

TOOLTIP:HealthBars
"Smart shows a bar over anything hurt, plus the selection and whatever is under the cursor. Selection only is what retail did."
END

GUI:OptionsGroupInput
"Input"
END

GUI:ChromaLighting
"Razer Chroma Lighting"
END

TOOLTIP:ChromaLighting
"During a match, a Razer keyboard, mouse and mousepad show the command bar, power, superweapons and money. In the menus Synapse keeps its own lighting."
END

GUI:OrderLines
"Order Lines"
END

TOOLTIP:OrderLines
"A line from each selected unit to where it is going, and on through every point it has queued. Off, a single order draws no line, but its marker and the ring where you click still show; a queued route keeps its line."
END

GUI:AircraftAltitudeLine
"Aircraft Altitude Lines"
END

TOOLTIP:AircraftAltitudeLine
"A thin line from each aircraft in the air straight down to the ground under it. Where it touches is where the plane really is, and its length is how high it flies. Parked aircraft have none."
END

GUI:SelectionOutlines
"Selection Outlines"
END

TOOLTIP:SelectionOutlines
"A glowing ring in its owner's color under each selected unit, and the same line around a selected building. Off, neither is drawn; order lines and the marks where you click stay."
END

GUI:PlayerColors
"Player Colors"
END

GUI:PlayerColors0
"Original"
END

GUI:PlayerColors1
"You, Allies, Enemies"
END

GUI:PlayerColors2
"By Team"
END

TOOLTIP:PlayerColors
"You, allies, enemies paints you blue, everyone on your side green and everyone shooting at you red. By team gives each alliance its own color and each member of it a shade. Your own screen only, so it changes nothing for anyone else in the game."
END

// Language - the Gameplay page's second group.  Each entry is written in its own language, so a
// player who cannot read the current one can still find theirs.

GUI:OptionsGroupLanguage
"Language"
END

GUI:Language
"Text Language"
END

GUI:Language0
"English"
END

GUI:Language1
"Türkçe"
END

GUI:Language2
"Deutsch"
END

GUI:Language3
"Українська"
END

GUI:Language4
"Русский"
END

GUI:Language5
"Français"
END

TOOLTIP:Language
"The language of menus, orders, briefings and subtitles. Voices and videos stay as installed. Takes effect the next time the game starts."
END

// The line under it when the lobby's Pile Limit has the pile closed to the player looking at it.

TOOLTIP:SupplyPileFull
"\n Taken: the pile limit keeps your gatherers out"
END

