GUI:Superweapons
"Superweapons"
END

GUI:SuperweaponsAllow
"Allow Superweapons"
END

GUI:SuperweaponsLimit
"Limit Superweapons"
END

GUI:SuperweaponsNone
"No Superweapons"
END

TOOLTIP:Superweapons
"How many superweapons a player may have standing. Allow: as many as he can pay for. Limit: one, and four for the USA Superweapon General. No: none at all, except the Superweapon General, who keeps one. He is the exception because his superweapons are what he pays for a weaker army with. Under No anyone, computer players too, may still put up one Nuclear Missile silo to buy China's upgrades in. It has no missile: no launch button, no countdown, no announcement."
END

GUI:StartShrouded
"Hidden Map"
END

GUI:DayNight
"Day/Night"
END

TOOLTIP:DayNight
"Night falls after every ten minutes of day, and at night every unit sees a fifth less far."
END

TOOLTIP:StartShrouded
"The map starts black for every player. Ground your side has not seen stays black until one of your units gets there, and the load screen does not give the start spots away. Off, everyone starts with the whole map in view under the fog, the way multiplayer has always played."
END

GUI:UnitLimit
"Unit Limit"
END

TOOLTIP:UnitLimit
"840 units shared out evenly between the players: two players get 420 each, eight get 105. Units standing and units waiting in a queue both count, buildings do not. Your own count and your share are in the top right corner during the match."
END

GUI:IncomeSharing
"Share Income"
END

TOOLTIP:IncomeSharing
"What allies split between them. Every payment is divided evenly between the player who earned it and each ally still in the match: an oil derrick paying 200 to one of two allies pays 100 to each. Oil Derricks shares captured derricks only. All Income adds supply runs, hackers and black markets."
END

GUI:IncomeSharingOff
"No Sharing"
END

GUI:IncomeSharingTech
"Oil Derricks"
END

GUI:IncomeSharingAll
"All Income"
END

GUI:TechRespawn
"Tech Respawn"
END

TOOLTIP:TechRespawn
"How long a destroyed tech building lies in ruins before a neutral one stands on the same spot again, at full health and ready to be captured. Oil derricks, refineries, hospitals, artillery platforms, repair bays and reinforcement pads all come back. A unit or a building standing on the spot holds it back until it moves."
END

GUI:TechRespawnOff
"Never"
END

GUI:TechRespawnFormat
"After %d min"
END

GUI:SupplyPileLimit
"Pile Limit"
END

TOOLTIP:SupplyPileLimit
"How many players may gather from one supply dock or supply pile at the same time. With 1, a pile belongs to whoever reaches it first, and every other player's supply trucks, Workers and Chinooks go to another pile or wait at home. Allies count as separate players. A pile is free again a minute after the last load was taken from it."
END

GUI:SupplyPileLimitOff
"No Limit"
END

GUI:SupplyPileLimitFormat
"%d per pile"
END

GUI:ProRules
"Pro Rules"
END

TOOLTIP:ProRules
"The tournament list. No Particle Cannon or SCUD Storm, except the Superweapon General's one cannon. The Nuclear Missile silo goes up but never fires. No Aurora, no Tactical Nuke MiGs, no demo bike, no suicide bombs, Neutron Shells or Stealth Comanche, and no Carpet Bomb before rank 3. A Microwave Tank cannot freeze a building still going up, nobody builds within 300 of an enemy building, and nobody puts more than two Patriots, Gatling Cannons or Stinger Sites round one group of oil derricks."
END

GUI:GameSpeed
"Game Speed"
END

TOOLTIP:GameSpeed
"How fast the skirmish runs. 1.0x is the original game and the speed of LAN matches, 1.5x the speed of online rooms. Ranked and Play vs AI play the speed picked before the match. Only the pace changes."
END

TOOLTIP:RoomGameSpeed
"Match speed, picked by the host"
END

GUI:GameSpeedMissions
"Game Speed in Missions"
END

TOOLTIP:GameSpeedMissions
"How fast campaign and Generals' Challenge missions run. 1.0x is the original game. The speed is set as a mission starts, so a change takes effect from the next one. A skirmish picks its own speed in the lobby."
END

